{# WHERE FILES GO — /files/settings.

   STATIC TWIN of the settled design's files/settings.html.

   READ-ONLY TRUTH FROM CONFIGURATION. Every line here is a fact about THIS
   deployment — which places are configured, which module's files go where, what
   is allowed in, how big one file may be. Nothing on it is a sample and nothing
   is aspirational: a settings page that shows what a different deployment would
   look like is worse than no settings page. It changes nothing either; where the
   bytes live is a deployment decision, not a form. #}
{% extends '@UhifadhiStorage/base.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}Where files go{% endblock %}

{% block shell_breadcrumbs %}<a href="/">uhifadhi</a> / <a href="{{ hubUrl }}">files</a> / where files go{% endblock %}

{# THE HEADER IS THE SECTION'S, NOT THIS SCREEN'S — the title is "Files" on
   every screen of the section and the strip says which one you are on. This
   one is a configure SECTION (`Storage targets`), so the strip above it is
   the section list rather than the four data tabs, written by the frame.

   NO "BACK TO FILES" ACTION. The one Configure entry lights here and is the
   way back; a module that typed a second door would be the only place in the
   product with two. #}
{% block shell_page_title %}Files{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_subtitle %}Which named places the organization keeps its files in, and what is allowed in.{% endblock %}

{% block storage_page %}



{% import '@UhifadhiStorage/files/_target.html.twig' as tgt %}

<h2 class="zone">The target</h2>
{# ONE TARGET, AND THIS IS IT. An installation writes to exactly one named
   place; the others it configured are where a switch can GO, and the one it
   is emptying is read-only until the count reaches zero. #}
{% if current %}
    <div class="f-store on">
        <div class="hd"><span class="f-be {{ current.kind == 's3' ? 's3' : 'local' }}"><i></i>{{ current.label }}</span><b>{{ current.what }}</b>{% if current.where %}<span class="where">{{ current.where }}</span>{% endif %}</div>
        {% if current.quotaBytes %}
            {% set filled = (held.bytes / current.quotaBytes * 100)|round(1) %}
            <div class="f-userow"><div class="top"><span class="sub">{{ held.bytes|storage_bytes }} of the {{ current.quotaBytes|storage_bytes }} bought</span><span class="n">{{ filled }}%</span></div>
                <div class="f-bar"><i style="width:{{ min(filled, 100) }}%"></i></div></div>
        {% endif %}
        <div class="rln"><span>Holding</span><span class="mono" style="font-size:11px">{{ held.files|number_format(0, '.', ' ') }} files &middot; {{ held.bytes|storage_bytes }}</span></div>
        <div class="rln"><span>Reachable without the app</span><span><span class="chip fail">never</span></span></div>
        {# Private by CONSTRUCTION: there is no visibility setting and no
           public-URL setting to get wrong, because there is no public URL. #}
        {# Private by CONSTRUCTION: there is no visibility setting and no
           public-URL setting to get wrong, because there is no public URL. #}
        <div class="use"><b>Nothing here is public.</b> Originals live outside the web root &middot; every module writes here, nothing chooses for itself.</div>
        {{ tgt.state(state, current, retired, alternatives, move, remaining, canClear, rate, secondsLeft, targetToken) }}
    </div>
{% else %}
    <div class="c"><div class="rln"><span class="d">No storage is configured, so nothing can be written.</span></div></div>
{% endif %}

<h2 class="zone">Which module&rsquo;s files go where</h2>
<div class="c">
    <span class="tab">The map<span class="src">&middot; one line per module</span></span>
    {# A module does not choose a storage; the HOST tells it which named place to
       use, and the module writes there. That is the whole arrangement. #}
    <div class="f-map">
        {% for row in map %}
            <div class="cellL"><i class="{{ row.slug }}" style="width:7px;height:7px;border-radius:2px;display:inline-block"></i> {{ row.label }} &mdash; {{ row.attachesTo }}</div>
            <div class="arrow"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"/><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"/></svg></div>
            <div class="cellR">{% if row.place %}<span class="f-be {{ row.place.kind == 's3' ? 's3' : 'local' }}"><i></i>{{ row.place.label }}</span>{% else %}<span class="chip idle">nowhere yet</span>{% endif %}</div>
        {% else %}
            <div class="cellL"><span class="d">No module has put its files on the hub yet</span></div>
            <div class="arrow"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"/><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"/></svg></div>
            <div class="cellR"><span class="chip idle">no module yet</span></div>
        {% endfor %}
    </div>
    {# Which is what lets one deployment run on a disk, another on object storage,
       and a third on something nobody has written yet, with no change inside any
       module. #}
    <div class="use"><b>A module never names a place.</b> It asks for its place; the installation answers.</div>
</div>

<h2 class="zone">How long things are kept, and what is allowed in</h2>
<div class="grid g2">
    <div class="c">
        <span class="tab">Keeping</span>
        <div class="rln"><span>Evidence on any record</span><span class="mono acc" style="font-size:11px">kept, always</span></div>
        <div class="rln"><span>Small pictures</span><span class="mono" style="font-size:11px">re-makeable at any time, never precious</span></div>
        <div class="rln"><span>When a record is removed</span><span class="mono" style="font-size:11px">its files go with it, in the same breath</span></div>
        <div class="rln"><span>When a file is removed</span><span class="mono" style="font-size:11px">the record keeps a line saying so</span></div>
        <div class="rln"><span>Who decides a removal</span><span class="mono" style="font-size:11px">the owning record, never this page</span></div>
        {# No sweeper deletes old photographs at midnight, and none will until somebody
           writes a retention rule down and an administrator switches it on. #}
        <div class="use" style="margin-bottom:0"><b>Nothing expires by itself.</b> Kept means kept.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="c">
        <span class="tab">What is allowed in</span>
        <div class="rln"><span>Photographs</span><span class="mono" style="font-size:11px">{{ allowed.photos|join(' · ') ?: '—' }}</span></div>
        <div class="rln"><span>Documents</span><span class="mono" style="font-size:11px">{{ allowed.documents|join(' · ') ?: '—' }}</span></div>
        <div class="rln"><span>Tracks</span><span class="mono" style="font-size:11px">{{ allowed.tracks|join(' · ') ?: '—' }}</span></div>
        <div class="rln"><span>Anything else</span><span class="mono r" style="font-size:11px">refused at the door</span></div>
        <div class="rln"><span>How the type is decided</span><span class="mono acc" style="font-size:11px">by reading the file, not its name</span></div>
        <div class="rln"><span>Biggest one file</span><span class="mono" style="font-size:11px">{{ maxBytes|storage_bytes }}</span></div>
        <div class="rln"><span>Small picture</span><span class="mono" style="font-size:11px">one, ~{{ thumbnailLongEdge }}px on the long side</span></div>
        {# Anyone can call a program "photo.jpg". It is also why a HEIC is kept even
           where no small picture could be made from it: it really is a photograph,
           simply one this machine cannot read. #}
        <div class="use" style="margin-bottom:0"><b>The name is evidence of nothing.</b> The type is detected, then checked against the list.</div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="c" style="margin-top:20px">
    <span class="tab">What an administrator can change here<span class="src">&middot; and what they cannot</span></span>
    <div class="grid g2" style="margin-bottom:0">
        <div>
            <div class="rln"><span>Point the platform at another place</span><span class="chip acc">yes &mdash; in configuration</span></div>
            <div class="rln"><span>Narrow what is allowed in</span><span class="chip acc">yes &mdash; in configuration</span></div>
            <div class="rln"><span>Change how big one file may be</span><span class="chip acc">yes &mdash; in configuration</span></div>
            <div class="rln"><span>Change the small picture&rsquo;s size</span><span class="chip acc">yes &mdash; in configuration</span></div>
        </div>
        <div>
            <div class="rln"><span>Make a file public</span><span class="chip fail">never</span></div>
            <div class="rln"><span>Remove evidence a record is holding</span><span class="chip fail">never &mdash; the record decides</span></div>
            <div class="rln"><span>Change what a file is</span><span class="chip fail">never &mdash; an original is untouchable</span></div>
            <div class="rln"><span>See a file whose record they cannot see</span><span class="chip fail">never</span></div>
        </div>
    </div>
    {# This page never becomes a back door into evidence. #}
    <div class="use"><b>Administering where bytes live is not being allowed to read them.</b></div>
</div>

    {# ONE HINT, AT THE BOTTOM, IN THE SHELL'S MARKUP. It used to be a lead
       above the content, which is where everybody reads it on every visit
       forever; the person still wondering who may open this page is the one
       who has already read the page. #}
    {{ include('@Shell/_page_hint.html.twig', {
        lead: 'Only an administrator opens this page.',
        say: 'Seeing where files are kept is seeing something about every file at once, so it rides on the same permission as installing a module.',
    }) }}
{% endblock %}
